From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Route 203's forest south of it: the same from Jubilife City
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0096 drew the route's forest on over the scenery map south of it,
and hid that map, only while both were loaded, and only 8 tiles deep. From
Jubilife City (that scenery map is east of it) the route's map is let go as
the player walks south: the forest east of the TV tower changed, trees gone
and back, and past the copies' 8 tiles there was black (a test run of
2026-11-06, two photos). It now goes by the scenery map alone: while it's
loaded, the route's strip by its south edge is read for it (as the maps
beside the loaded ones are: its own copy, its own render object, 2 kept)
and drawn again over the scenery map's whole depth, 16 copies, each only
while its box is in the view. So it's the same whether the route's map is
loaded or not. On the route itself nothing changes (the same pictures as
0096 at 216-252,763).

---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index 20eeb353..274ab489 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
@@ -2464,6 +2464,13 @@ static const u16 sPortEdgeAboveScenery[] = {
 // the scenery map south of it isn't drawn: by the route's west map its
 // forest overlapped the route's last trees and the copies, trees in each
 // other with a light line between (a photo of 2026-11-06 at 228,763).
